# SmartMediLink OOSD & Architecture Rules

## 1. Core OOP & Inheritance
- [cite_start]**Abstract Foundation:** Always use the `AppUser` abstract class (`lib/models/app_user.dart`) for user-related logic[cite: 88].
- [cite_start]**Polymorphism:** Use the `saveToFirestore()` override in `Assistant` and `Seeker` instead of manual role checks[cite: 88, 15].
- [cite_start]**Encapsulation:** Keep sensitive data (NIC, Address, Job IDs) private with `_` and use getters for read-only access[cite: 64, 65, 90].

## 2. Business Logic & Behavioral States
- [cite_start]**Assistant Lifecycle:** Respect the states: `Unverified` -> `Active` (after Admin approval) -> `Available`/`Matched`/`Booked`[cite: 175, 181, 191].
- [cite_start]**Service Continuity:** When modifying bookings, implement the "Identify Nearest Backup" logic if the primary Assistant is unavailable[cite: 53, 54, 163].
- [cite_start]**Matching Engine:** New "Jobs" created by Seekers must be modeled as distinct objects that the Matching Engine uses to alert Assistants[cite: 15, 18, 146].

## 3. Flutter & Firebase Implementation
- [cite_start]**Role-Based Routing:** Use the `AuthGate` in `login.dart` as the central router based on `registrationComplete` status and user role[cite: 94].
- [cite_start]**Data Persistence:** Use `fromFirestore` factory methods to instantiate objects; never use raw Maps in the UI[cite: 70].
- **Validation:** Assistant registration must validate NIC (length > 6) and require at least one skill and one working day.

## 4. Cursor Interaction Guidelines
- [cite_start]**Project Report Alignment:** Before suggesting changes, cross-reference the Sequence and Activity diagrams in the Project Report[cite: 135, 121].
- **Explanation First:** Cursor must explain how a proposed change maintains the OOSD model before writing code.

## 5. Cloud Functions & Backend Logic
- **Matching Engine:** The primary matching logic must reside in `functions/src/matching.ts`.
- **Trigger Type:** Use `onDocumentCreated` for the `jobs` collection to trigger the matching engine.
- **Admin SDK:** Use `firebase-admin` to query the `users` collection for available Assistants.
- **Algorithm:** The engine must filter by `skills`, `workingTimes`, and `isVerified == true`.